  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "title: \"Chapter 11: Survival Analysis - Lab part 2\" \n",
        "categories: [lab,python]\n",
        "date: 2024-09-03\n",
        "format:\n",
        "   html:\n",
        "      page-layout: full\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "# Survival Analysis {#sec-survival-analysis}\n",
        "\n",
        "We begin by importing some of our libraries at this top level.\n"
      ],
      "id": "709a6444"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "from matplotlib.pyplot import subplots\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "from ISLP.models import ModelSpec as MS\n",
        "from ISLP import load_data\n",
        "from lifelines import KaplanMeierFitter, CoxPHFitter\n",
        "from lifelines.statistics import logrank_test, multivariate_logrank_test\n",
        "from ISLP.survival import sim_time\n",
        "\n",
        "km = KaplanMeierFitter()\n",
        "coxph = CoxPHFitter"
      ],
      "id": "c2b99acf",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Publication Data {#sec-pub}\n",
        "\n",
        "The  `Publication`  data   presented in Section~\\ref{sec:pub}  can be found in the `ISLP` package.\n",
        "We first reproduce Figure~\\ref{fig:lauersurv}  by plotting the Kaplan-Meier curves stratified on the  `posres`  variable, which records whether the study had a positive or negative result.\n"
      ],
      "id": "a217c95f"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "fig, ax = subplots(figsize=(8,8))\n",
        "Publication = load_data('Publication')\n",
        "by_result = {}\n",
        "for result, df in Publication.groupby('posres'):\n",
        "    by_result[result] = df\n",
        "    km_result = km.fit(df['time'], df['status'])\n",
        "    km_result.plot(label='Result=%d' % result, ax=ax)"
      ],
      "id": "9a6002f2",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "As discussed previously, the $p$-values from fitting Cox’s\n",
        "proportional hazards model to the `posres` variable are quite\n",
        "large, providing no evidence of a difference in time-to-publication\n",
        "between studies with positive versus negative results.\n"
      ],
      "id": "f0721056"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "posres_df = MS(['posres',\n",
        "                'time',\n",
        "                'status'],\n",
        "                intercept=False).fit_transform(Publication)\n",
        "posres_fit = coxph().fit(posres_df,\n",
        "                         'time',\n",
        "                         'status')\n",
        "posres_fit.summary[['coef', 'se(coef)', 'p']]"
      ],
      "id": "25036942",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "However, the results change dramatically when we include other\n",
        "predictors in the model. Here we exclude the funding mechanism\n",
        "variable.\n"
      ],
      "id": "a7cda139"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "model = MS(Publication.columns.drop('mech'),\n",
        "           intercept=False)\n",
        "coxph().fit(model.fit_transform(Publication),\n",
        "            'time',\n",
        "            'status').summary[['coef', 'se(coef)', 'p']]"
      ],
      "id": "561a9f46",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "We see that there are a number of statistically significant variables,\n",
        "including whether the trial focused on a clinical endpoint, the impact\n",
        "of the study, and whether the study had positive or negative results.\n"
      ],
      "id": "d7df2cbb"
    }
  ],
